        <para id="para-00031" class="custom-question-container"><span class="custom-question-number">7. </span>Are the patterns you noticed still happening? See if you can apply those patterns to
          the following equations.</para>

      <exercise id="_8fd2bb2b-35a9-49b3-93e0-6b1010b68b27" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00020">
          <para id="para-00070">a. For the equation <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo>
                <m:mn>5</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>, what is the <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>-coordinate of the vertex?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00020">
          <para id="para-00071">The <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>-coordinate of the vertex
            of this equation is <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>.</para>
        
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_97021ac7-5208-432a-a6f5-432c6448485f" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00021">
          <para id="para-00074">b. For the equation <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo>
                <m:mn>5</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>, what is the <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>-coordinate of the vertex?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00021">
          <para id="para-00075">The <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>-coordinate of the vertex
            of this equation is <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo>
                <m:mn>5</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>.</para>

        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_1d9cfcdf-595c-471d-9307-16dd20ce2f36" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00022">
          <para id="para-00077">c. For the equation <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo>
                <m:mn>5</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>, does the graph open up
            or down?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00022">
          <para id="para-00078">The graph opens upward. The squared term has a positive
            coefficient <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>.</para>
      
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_16199d79-2505-408f-b4ff-e5b931fa83bb" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00023">
          <para id="para-00081">d. For the equation <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>100</m:mn>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>50</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>, what is the <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>-coordinate of the vertex?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00023">
          <para id="para-00082">The <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>-coordinate of the vertex
            of this equation is <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo>
                <m:mn>100</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>.</para>
        
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="a1771807-d7bb-465d-9019-eabb1fce4737" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00024">
          <para id="para-00085">e. For the equation <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>100</m:mn>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>50</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>, what is the <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>-coordinate of the vertex?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00024">
          <para id="para-00086">The <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>-coordinate of the vertex
            of this equation is <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mn>50</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_7fc8f227-f6be-48a3-97bf-c9787f891f76" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00025">
          <para id="para-00088">f. For the equation <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>100</m:mn>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>50</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>, does the graph open up
            or down?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00025">
          <para id="para-00089">The graph opens downward. The squared term has a negative
            coefficient <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo>
                <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>.</para>
         
        </solution>
      </exercise>


